          {
            title: 'Tute individual',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Tute for two players; no partnerships. Standard 40-card Spanish deck. Ten cards each, stock with face-up trump; follow suit and overtake; Cantes (40/20) after winning a trick; Tute (4 Kings or 4 Knights) wins the deal. Most points in the deal wins that game; session is multiple deals.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Originated in Italy (as tutti); spread to Spain in the 19th century where it became one of the most popular card games. Two-player individual variant.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two players (or three).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard Spanish pack of 40 cards: four suits (Swords/espadas, Batons/bastos, Cups/copas, Coins/oros). Ranks and point values: Ace 11, Three 10, King 4, Horse 3, Jack 2; Seven through Two count zero. One suit is trump each deal, determined by the face-up card.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '10 each, next card face up for trump, remainder as stock; after each trick winner draws first then others anticlockwise.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
